# Time-dependent phenomena — DTU 10112

Two self-contained marimo notebooks for Advanced Quantum Mechanics, following
Ballentine pp. 332–349 and the course's time-dependence slides.

## Open and experiment

### Spin-1/2: precession and magnetic resonance

[![Open in molab](https://marimo.io/molab-shield.svg)](https://molab.marimo.io/github/mbrandbyge-DTU/Advanced-Quantum-Mechanics-10112/blob/main/TimeDependence/spin_dynamics.py/wasm)

Set the initial spin, static and rotating fields, and the observation frame.
Compare laboratory and rotating-frame trajectories on the Bloch sphere, and
measure the spin-flip probability. The notebook uses the slides' convention:
`H = -(omega_0 sigma_z + rotating term)/2`, so resonance is `omega = -omega_0`.

### Tight-binding chains: transfer, decay, and the Zeno effect

[![Open in molab](https://marimo.io/molab-shield.svg)](https://molab.marimo.io/github/mbrandbyge-DTU/Advanced-Quantum-Mechanics-10112/blob/main/TimeDependence/chain_dynamics.py/wasm)

Change chain length, the first hopping, the end-site energy, and the initial state.
Explore two-site oscillations, escape into a long chain, reflections, Gaussian
wave packets, and ideal repeated projective measurements.

